def num_analysis_cubature_genz_malik_compiled(a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5, *, session=None, checked=False):
    """
    Native Genz-Malik cubature: physical same-unit coordinates, independently measured output, explicit evaluation limit and volume-dimensioned absolute tolerance. Adaptive Genz-Malik cubature over the box `[lo, hi]`. Each region is integrated with the degree-7 Genz-Malik rule (`1 + 4n + 2n(n-1) + 2^n` points) whose embedded degree-5 rule gives the error estimate; the region with the largest error is bisected along the axis with the largest fourth divided difference. The box is first split uniformly into a few sub-boxes so that narrow peaks are not missed. Stops when the total error is below `max(abs_tol, rel_tol * |value|)` or after `max_evals` integrand evaluations (`converged == false`). Intended for 2 to about 8 dimensions. A bisection only replaces a region by its two halves, so the regions always tile the box exactly: their volumes sum to the box volume and no two overlap. `value` and `error` are the sums of the region values and of the region estimates; the estimate is the embedded degree-5/7 difference, a heuristic rather than a rigorous bound (see the module limitations).
    Returns an unevaluated term; call ``Session.compute`` to reduce it.
    Pass ``checked=True`` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.
    """
    return (_call if checked else _apply)("num_analysis_cubature_genz_malik_compiled", (a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5), session)


