def num_analysis_monte_carlo_stratified_compiled(a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5, a6, *, session=None, checked=False):
    """
    Native stratified Monte Carlo with checked exponential grid/sample cost and independent physical output units. Stratified Monte Carlo integral over `[lo, hi]`. Every axis is cut into `strata_per_axis` equal cells, so the box has `strata_per_axis^dim` strata and each stratum receives `per_stratum` uniform samples. The estimator is the volume-weighted sum of the stratum means and the error is the root of the sum of the squared stratum standard errors, which is unbiased and never assumes that the strata are equally variable. Stratification removes the between-stratum part of the variance, so it pays when the integrand is smooth on the scale of a cell (the within-cell variance falls like the square of the cell width) and buys nothing when the integrand varies inside every cell, as a discontinuity finer than the grid does. The cost is exponential in the dimension: `strata^dim * per_stratum` evaluations. Arguments below one are treated as one. Returns `converged = false` with a `NaN` value and no evaluations when `strata_per_axis^dim * per_stratum` does not fit in a `usize`.
    Returns an unevaluated term; call ``Session.compute`` to reduce it.
    Pass ``checked=True`` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.
    """
    return (_call if checked else _apply)("num_analysis_monte_carlo_stratified_compiled", (a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5, a6), session)


