def num_grid_fem_error_indicators(a0, a1, a2, a3, *, session=None, checked=False):
    """
    Native simplex finite-element method with explicit geometry/time/field references. Diffusivity is normalized by L²/T, reaction by1/T, source by U/T; compiled callbacks use coherent coordinates and retained physical output domains. Mesh/DOF/refinement/callback work bounds are checked. Residual error indicators `η_T`, one per cell, of a P1 or P2 solution. `η_T² = h_T² ∫_T (f(t,·) - c u_h + ∇·(k ∇u_h))² dx + Σ_{e ⊂ ∂T} ½ h_e ∫_e [k ∂_n u_h]² ds`, with `h_T` and `h_e` the diameters of the cell and of its faces. The face sum runs over interior faces only, so the estimator measures the discretisation error of the differential equation, not the approximation of non-homogeneous boundary data. For P1 the element term is `f - c u_h` (`∇·(k ∇u_h) = 0`); for P2 the constant `k Δu_h` is included. In 1D the face term is empty (the jump lives on a set of measure zero).
    Returns an unevaluated term; call ``Session.compute`` to reduce it.
    Pass ``checked=True`` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.
    """
    return (_call if checked else _apply)("num_grid_fem_error_indicators", (a0, a1, a2, a3), session)


